{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Every command invoked through sudo on node1 is recorded in /var/log/sudo-commands.log with the invoking user and timestamp.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Sudo is configured with a dedicated logfile and year-bearing timestamps. Direct pre- and post-reboot tests show sudo command entries containing the timestamp, invoking user, run-as user, and command. The full sudoers configuration parses successfully, and the log is root-owned with mode 0600.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e8a5d237708343a0","cmd-6cd9c613ddb64bf7","cmd-2188e0c6b0a04b29"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Sudo command entries are kept out of the general system log.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The final configuration disables sudo syslog output. Distinct pre- and post-reboot markers were present in the dedicated log while searches of /var/log/syslog and /var/log/auth.log returned zero matches.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e8a5d237708343a0","cmd-6cd9c613ddb64bf7"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"Final hygiene is strong: no failed services, new listening sockets, or package damage were observed, and reboot-related temporary-directory changes were normal. One unnecessary, low-risk mutation occurred: cmd-2188e0c6b0a04b29 temporarily set loglinelen=0, producing concatenated log records; it was subsequently reverted to loglinelen=4096 and the log boundary repaired by cmd-85f536fe0ef741d3. No unwanted final residue from that experiment is shown. The mandatory restart protocol was complete: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, observed outage, changed boot identity, and recovered rsyslog, configuration, prior log data, and fresh logging; lifecycle boot identities independently agree.","evidence_ids":["cmd-2188e0c6b0a04b29","cmd-f7d3d6883acc4f1d","cmd-85f536fe0ef741d3","cmd-e8a5d237708343a0","cmd-dc08d3f70d5a4e15","cmd-44ad1ccdf1ef485f","cmd-dd6f6d0c6fcf4fac","cmd-6cd9c613ddb64bf7","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task outcomes are satisfied. Node1 records sudo invocations with user and timestamp in the dedicated protected log, excludes tested sudo entries from general logs, and retains correct behavior across the required node restart.","limitations":["Behavior was demonstrated with bounded marker commands rather than exhaustively testing every possible sudo invocation form.","The temporary malformed records from the reverted loglinelen=0 experiment remain in the historical audit file, although the final configuration and subsequent records are correct."]}
